  62:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  63:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
  64:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****                  ##### Peripheral extended features functions #####
  65:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
  66:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  67:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     *** Main and Backup Regulators configuration ***
  68:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     ================================================
  69:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     [..] 
  70:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The backup domain includes 4 Kbytes of backup SRAM accessible only from 
  71:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           the CPU, and address in 32-bit, 16-bit or 8-bit mode. Its content is 
  72:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           retained even in Standby or VBAT mode when the low power backup regulator
  73:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           is enabled. It can be considered as an internal EEPROM when VBAT is 
  74:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           always present. You can use the HAL_PWREx_EnableBkUpReg() function to 
  75:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           enable the low power backup regulator. 
  76:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  77:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) When the backup domain is supplied by VDD (analog switch connected to VDD) 
  78:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           the backup SRAM is powered from VDD which replaces the VBAT power supply to 
  79:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           save battery life.
  80:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  81:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The backup SRAM is not mass erased by a tamper event. It is read 
  82:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           protected to prevent confidential data, such as cryptographic private 
  83:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           key, from being accessed. The backup SRAM can be erased only through 
  84:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           the Flash interface when a protection level change from level 1 to 
  85:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           level 0 is requested. 
  86:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       -@- Refer to the description of Read protection (RDP) in the Flash 
  87:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           programming manual.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Temp\ccknCFEt.s 			page 3


  88:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  89:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The main internal regulator can be configured to have a tradeoff between 
  90:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           performance and power consumption when the device does not operate at 
  91:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           the maximum frequency. This is done through __HAL_PWR_MAINREGULATORMODE_CONFIG() 
  92:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           macro which configure VOS bit in PWR_CR register
  93:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           
  94:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****         Refer to the product datasheets for more details.
  95:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  96:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     *** FLASH Power Down configuration ****
  97:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     =======================================
  98:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     [..] 
  99:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) By setting the FPDS bit in the PWR_CR register by using the 
 100:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           HAL_PWREx_EnableFlashPowerDown() function, the Flash memory also enters power 
 101:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           down mode when the device enters Stop mode. When the Flash memory 
 102:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           is in power down mode, an additional startup delay is incurred when 
 103:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           waking up from Stop mode.
 104:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           
 105:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx/446xx/469xx/479xx Devices, the scale can be modified only when
 106:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            is OFF and the HSI or HSE clock source is selected as system clock. 
 107:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            The new value programmed is active only when the PLL is ON.
 108:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            When the PLL is OFF, the voltage scale 3 is automatically selected. 
 109:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****         Refer to the datasheets for more details.
 110:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
 111:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     *** Over-Drive and Under-Drive configuration ****
 112:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     =================================================
 113:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     [..]         
 114:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx/446xx/469xx/479xx Devices, in Run mode: the main regulator has
 115:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            2 operating modes available:
 116:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****         (++) Normal mode: The CPU and core logic operate at maximum frequency at a given 
 117:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****              voltage scaling (scale 1, scale 2 or scale 3)
 118:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****         (++) Over-drive mode: This mode allows the CPU and the core logic to operate at a 
 119:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****             higher frequency than the normal mode for a given voltage scaling (scale 1,  
 120:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****             scale 2 or scale 3). This mode is enabled through HAL_PWREx_EnableOverDrive() function 
 121:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****             disabled by HAL_PWREx_DisableOverDrive() function, to enter or exit from Over-drive mod
 122:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****             the sequence described in Reference manual.
 123:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****              
 124:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx/446xx/469xx/479xx Devices, in Stop mode: the main regulator or low
 125:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            supplies a low power voltage to the 1.2V domain, thus preserving the content of register
 126:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            and internal SRAM. 2 operating modes are available:
 127:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****          (++) Normal mode: the 1.2V domain is preserved in nominal leakage mode. This mode is only 
 128:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****               available when the main regulator or the low power regulator is used in Scale 3 or 
 129:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****               low voltage mode.
 130:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****          (++) Under-drive mode: the 1.2V domain is preserved in reduced leakage mode. This mode is 
 131:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****               available when the main regulator or the low power regulator is in low voltage mode.
 132:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
 133:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** @endverbatim
 134:board/stm32f401rct6/Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****   * @{
